---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Headless Website &amp; API-First Development | Kelp"
  description="Headless WordPress, Shopify Hydrogen, and API-First website development for organizations whose content and customer experience need more flexibility."
  darkHeader={true}
>
  <article>
    <SimpleHero
      title="Headless"
      description="We build headless experiences that separate the frontend from the backend so each layer can do what it does best. The result is complete control over the user experience, plus the performance gains that come from a leaner frontend."
      dark={true}
    />

    <section class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <div class="platform">
        <div class="platform-logo platform-logo--headless">
          <span class="platform-badge">Headless</span>
          <p class="platform-caption">WordPress, Shopify, and custom APIs</p>
        </div>

        <div class="platform-text">
          <p>
            Headless works with any platform or CMS that exposes APIs. That can
            mean WordPress, Shopify, a Google Spreadsheet, or a custom backend
            built around the tools your team already uses. The point is not to
            replace the system behind the site, but to give the frontend
            complete freedom to shape the experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            The primary reason to go headless is control. You get to design the
            interface without CMS constraints, and you get a faster site because
            the frontend only ships what it needs. That usually means better
            performance, cleaner interactions, and a system that can grow
            without becoming tangled.
          </p>
          <p>
            We keep the implementation practical. If you already have a CMS,
            commerce stack, spreadsheet workflow, or other API-backed system in
            place, we can help turn it into a cleaner, more flexible frontend
            experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/contact/" class="button">
              Talk to us about a headless build
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="service-body">
      <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
        <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
        <p>
          Headless projects can fail when architecture is chosen before the
          editor, customer, and integration requirements are understood. A
          custom front end may be fast and flexible yet leave the marketing team
          unable to publish or the developer team responsible for too many
          moving parts.
        </p>
        <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
        <p>
          We compare conventional and headless approaches against content
          workflow, integrations, performance, search access, hosting, and
          support. When headless is justified, we model the data and delivery
          path before building the interface. We also plan how failures and
          updates will be handled after launch.
        </p>
        <h2>Choose Architecture for the Work</h2>
        <p>
          We map the content model, customer journeys, integrations, editor
          workflow, performance needs, and ongoing ownership before choosing a
          framework. The site still has to be maintainable, accessible, and
          clear to search systems. A technically impressive front end is not
          useful if the team cannot update it or important content cannot be
          discovered.
        </p>
        <h2>Connect the Right Systems</h2>
        <p>
          Headless projects may join a CMS, storefront, search service, CRM,
          product data source, or custom application through APIs. We define
          which system owns the information, how it is delivered, and what
          happens when a service fails. Kelp's own site is described on its
          WordPress platform page as a headless WordPress instance. Kelp has
          also published headless Astro work and Shopify Hydrogen capabilities.
        </p>
        <h2>Use the Simplest Architecture That Meets the Goal</h2>
        <p>
          Many businesses can achieve what they need with a well-built theme and
          thoughtful integrations. We compare the tradeoffs before proposing a
          headless approach. Talk with Kelp about the experience and systems you
          need to connect.
        </p>
        <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Architecture and platform decision</li>
          <li>API and content-model planning</li>
          <li>Custom front-end development</li>
          <li>Search, editor, deployment, and support review</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
        <p>
          Bring the experience you want to create and the systems it must draw
          from. We can recommend whether the added flexibility of headless
          development is worth its maintenance cost.
        </p>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <h3>Will a headless site be better for SEO?</h3>
        <p>
          Architecture alone does not make a page useful or discoverable.
          Content access, rendering, links, performance, and page quality still
          need to be planned and checked.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
            Talk Through Your Project
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style lang="scss">
  .platform {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 2rem 6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--teal);

    &:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    &-logo {
      flex: 0 1 220px;
      text-align: center;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
      order: 2;

      @media (max-width: 767px) {
        margin: auto;
      }
    }

    &-logo--headless {
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    &-text {
      flex: 1 1 500px;
    }
  }

  .platform-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--teal);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-family: var(--sans-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: white;
  }

  .platform-caption {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sans-serif);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--black);
  }
</style>
